=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_REMOVED
title: `match=` added to a bare `pytest.raises(ValueError)` is the same raise, checked more strictly
origin: #434 B, ruling 434 B (2026-10-16) - the bare call pairs with the new `match=` call of the same callee, expected types and other keywords, in a pass after the order fallback; it read as ASSERT_REMOVED (strength UNKNOWN), held at warn
=== before: tests/test_paths.py ===
import pytest

from app import create


def test_relative_path_rejected():
    with pytest.raises(ValueError):
        create("relative/path")
=== after: tests/test_paths.py ===
import pytest

from app import create


def test_relative_path_rejected():
    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match="must be absolute"):
        create("relative/path")
